WEBVTT

00:41:56.329 --> 00:42:00.663
Right. But, you know, to make yourself
ready for that kind of relationship,

00:42:01.538 --> 00:42:05.246
I wasn't walking the trail to do that. But
that was one of the outcomes of it.

00:42:05.413 --> 00:42:06.413
Yeah.

00:42:06.413 --> 00:42:09.079
You moved to Portland, you
got a job waiting tables.

00:42:09.079 --> 00:42:12.329
You started working full time, writing
your first novel, Torch,

00:42:12.329 --> 00:42:16.038
and you then went to graduate school
to Syracuse University and got

00:42:16.038 --> 00:42:20.413
a master of fine arts in fiction writing
so you could actually finish the book.

00:42:20.663 --> 00:42:22.079
Why? What made you decide to do that?

00:42:22.079 --> 00:42:26.204
What made you feel like that would help
you get to that moment that were where

00:42:26.204 --> 00:42:27.204
the book would be finished?

00:42:27.496 --> 00:42:29.996
Yeah, it was it was mostly financial.